From: Sumit Garg <sumit.garg@linaro.org>
Date: Wed, 20 Feb 2019 11:32:27 +0530
Subject: tee: fix possible error pointer ctx dereferencing
Git-commit: bb342f016862a0d5b013c2a9dce0f91412b0be77
Patch-mainline: v5.1-rc1
References: git-fixes

Add check for valid ctx pointer and then only dereference ctx to
configure supp_nowait flag.

Fixes: 42bf4152d8a7 ("tee: add supp_nowait flag in tee_context struct")
Reported-by: Dan Carpenter <dan.carpenter@oracle.com>
Signed-off-by: Sumit Garg <sumit.garg@linaro.org>
Signed-off-by: Arnd Bergmann <arnd@arndb.de>
Acked-by: Ivan T. Ivanov <iivanov@suse.de>
---
 drivers/tee/tee_core.c |    4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/tee/tee_core.c
+++ b/drivers/tee/tee_core.c
@@ -994,7 +994,9 @@ tee_client_open_context(struct tee_conte
 	 * tee_client_open_session() if any in kernel client requires
 	 * different behaviour.
 	 */
-	ctx->supp_nowait = true;
+	if (!IS_ERR(ctx))
+		ctx->supp_nowait = true;
+
 	return ctx;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(tee_client_open_context);
